From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:32:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 106/148] feat(refinery): merge-batch.sh keeps a collapsed head
 a batch of 1, land refuses 0-commit members, add serial (gcp-l8td.11)

Re-grounding the wiring bead (gcp-l8td.10) found two things merge-batch.sh must
do before the formula calls it. Both are script work, so they land here and the
formula bead stays wiring only. merge-batch.sh is still inert.

1. A collapsed head was batched, and land then closed it on someone else's
   commit (an M1 hole). The batch iteration runs land instead of merge-push.sh
   --work, so the head never met the single-bead merge-state gate. stack only
   checked the head's eligibility; when the head's rebase collapsed it recorded
   commits=0 with the target's tip and patch-id, land mapped it to the next
   member's commit, the patch-ids matched, and the head closed merged on another
   bead's sha. Fix at the root: after the head passes mb_check_member, stack
   asks branch_has_real_change; an empty rebase leaves a batch of 1 so
   merge-push.sh --work's gate decides it, and an unanswerable one degrades.
   land also refuses any 0-commit member (commits >= 1), since such a member has
   no commit of its own to record.

2. The batch-red stamping must be a script call, not formula shell (design trap
   5). `serial --head <id>` stamps every member with merge_batch_serial=<its
   origin/<branch> sha> (the value mb_check_member compares) and writes one
   note, so select leaves them out of a batch until their branch moves. It never
   writes rejection_reason, assignee or status and never closes a bead. A
   fetch/rev-parse/update failure puts the member in failed=; a note failure is
   a WARN. Whatever happened it then removes the manifest and cleans up temp.
   Exit 0 when all are stamped, 2 when any failed, 1 for a usage/config/manifest
   error; every exit ends with `merge-batch: RESULT <rc> serial=.. failed=..`.
   land's manifest checks moved into lb_read_manifest, shared by land and serial.

Validation: gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_batch.sh (next commit) passes 20
cases and its new cases fail against the previous script.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
